    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` and wrote 61 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. The function converts each input to `Decimal` (floats via `str()`, `bool` and other types raise `TypeError`), validates ranges and zone, and computes billable weight as the larger of actual and volumetric weight rounded up to 0.5 kg. It then applies the base charge, zone factor, free shipping for zones 1–2 at a subtotal of 150 or more, and the flat 12.00 oversize surcharge for a longest side above 120 cm. The total is quantized with `ROUND_HALF_UP` inside a higher-precision context. I could not run the coverage gate because only the test command was allowed, so the 90% threshold is unverified. By reading the code, I believe every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by the tests. I also treated NaN and infinite inputs as `ValueError`, which the spec does not state explicitly.",
